      "updated": 1757882230596,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements\n1. Design a session management system\n2. Should support revocation of active sessions of an user\n\nClarifying questions\n1. what is the scale ?\n    500M DAU\n2. what kind of client should be supported ? web, mobile, backend services ?\n    all of the above\n3. are the client geographically distributed ?\n    yes\n4. how large is the session data ?\n    few KB\n5. do we need to integrate with any existing identity providers ?\n    yes\n\nNon Functional Requirements\n1. Consistency,  \n    session revocation might need strong concistency for sensitive flows\n    might be able to get away with eventual concistency for others\n    system should be highly available\n2. Performance/Scalability,\n    latency for session validation (< 10ms)\n    latency for session creation/update (< 100ms)\n    should be able to support millions of sessions ops/s\n3. Security,\n    session data should be tamper proof\n    session data should be confidential\n4. Reliability,\n    should be fault tolerant to various kind of internal and external faults\n    implicit \n     \n\n \n        ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements\n1. Design a session management system\n2. Should support revocation of active sessions of an user\n\nClarifying questions\n1. what is the scale ?\n    500M DAU\n2. what kind of client should be supported ? web, mobile, backend services ?\n    all of the above\n3. are the client geographically distributed ?\n    yes\n4. how large is the session data ?\n    few KB\n5. do we need to integrate with any existing identity providers ?\n    yes\n\nNon Functional Requirements\n1. Consistency,  \n    session revocation might need strong concistency for sensitive flows\n    might be able to get away with eventual concistency for others\n    system should be highly available\n2. Performance/Scalability,\n    latency for session validation (< 10ms)\n    latency for session creation/update (< 100ms)\n    should be able to support millions of sessions ops/s\n3. Security,\n    session data should be tamper proof\n    session data should be confidential\n4. Reliability,\n    should be fault tolerant to various kind of internal and external faults\n    implicit \n     \n\n \n        ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
